==Evolution==
Evolves into '''UFO Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''The Flying Cat''' at level 20+10 using [[Normal Cat Capsule|Cat Tickets]].

==Strategy/Usage==
This cat can be useful in the early-game when most enemies have low range, allowing it to deal damage without getting killed. This is important, as his cost, health, and range quickly become his downfall once [[Empire of Cats]] is over.

If you don't yet have [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], you can use it for common boss enemies throughout Empire of Cats like Hippoe, Pigge, Jackie Peng and Gory. Make sure you send out cats with high health like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]] or [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]] because UFO Cat has a high knockback count.

Since this is a very situational unit due to its short range, don't prioritize this cat too much. While the levels will count towards your [[User Rank]], the real benefit of this cat is found in the [[Saucers (Combo)|Saucers]] [[Cat Combo]] (which then can be paired with [[Madam Bride (Rare Cat)|Madam Bride]] and Cupid Cat for [[Massive Damage|massive damage]] boosts). In later stages, this unit won't help much.

==='''True Form'''===
Due to the short range of The Flying Cat and its relatively low health, it is not recommended to use him against [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemies, even though he gains a chance to weaken them. The only Angel that The Flying Cat can effectively handle is [[Gabriel]]. At best, Flying might weaken [[Boraphim]] or [[Heavenly Hippoe]] as well, but it's still likely to die early, so you should instead rely on other attackers such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]].

Thanks to its somewhat high DPS, it can be useful in certain situations such as dealing with slow but powerful long-ranged enemies like [[THE SLOTH]], although high HP units like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]] may be preferred, depending on the level. Later in the game, it is outclassed by longer-ranged cats, especially [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and its [[:Category:Crazed Cats|Crazed]] counterpart [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Bird Cat]], due to having more range and higher DPS.

